    "content": "{\"title\": \"CT CORONARY ANGIO\", \"technique\": \"Technique:\", \"normal_findings\": [\"Past History of Surgery:\", \"Axial 0.5 mm thin CT sections were performed through the heart with ECG gating and intravenous non ionic contrast. Reconstructions were performed through R-R interval in systole and diastole. Three dimensional multiplanar and curved reconstructions performed through the coronary arteries were studied.\", \"Report:\", \"The coronary artery calcium score is .\", \"The coronary arterial system is right dominant.\", \"The Left main coronary artery (LMCA) reveals no significant stenosis. It bifurcates into anterior descending (LAD) and left circumflex (LCx).\", \"The proximal LAD reveals no significant stenosis. The mid and distal LAD reveals no significant stenosis.\", \"The diagonal arteries reveal no significant stenosis.\", \"The LCx and obtuse marginal (OM) branches reveal no significant stenosis.\", \"The proximal right coronary artery (RCA) reveals no significant stenosis. The mid and distal RCA reveal no significant stenosis.\", \"The posterior descending artery (PDA) and posterolateral branch reveals no significant stenosis.\", \"Myocardium reveals no focal thinning.\", \"Functional study:\", \"EF :\", \"EDV :\", \"ESV :\", \"SV :\", \"CO :\", \"Myocardial mass :\", \"Screening of the chest:\", \"Trachea and major bronchi are normal.\", \"Lungs show normal architexture and attenuation.\", \"There is no evidence of any focal pathology.\", \"There is no evidence of air entrapment or emphysema.\", \"The pleura appears normal.\"], \"default_impression\": \"IMPRESSION:###CT coronary angio findings reveal no significant stenosis in epicardial coronary arteries.\", \"raw_text\": \"CT CORONARY ANGIO\\nClinical Profile:\\nPast History of Surgery:\\nTechnique:\\nAxial 0.5 mm thin CT sections were performed through the heart with ECG gating and intravenous non ionic contrast. Reconstructions were performed through R-R interval in systole and diastole. Three dimensional multiplanar and curved reconstructions performed through the coronary arteries were studied.\\nReport:\\nThe coronary artery calcium score is .\\nThe coronary arterial system is right dominant.\\nThe Left main coronary artery (LMCA) reveals no significant stenosis. It bifurcates into anterior descending (LAD) and left circumflex (LCx).\\nThe proximal LAD reveals no significant stenosis. The mid and distal LAD reveals no significant stenosis.\\nThe diagonal arteries reveal no significant stenosis.\\nThe LCx and obtuse marginal (OM) branches reveal no significant stenosis.\\nThe proximal right coronary artery (RCA) reveals no significant stenosis. The mid and distal RCA reveal no significant stenosis.\\nThe posterior descending artery (PDA) and posterolateral branch reveals no significant stenosis.\\nMyocardium reveals no focal thinning.\\nFunctional study:\\nEF :\\nEDV :\\nESV :\\nSV :\\nCO :\\nMyocardial mass :\\nScreening of the chest:\\nTrachea and major bronchi are normal.\\nLungs show normal architexture and attenuation.\\nThere is no evidence of any focal pathology.\\nThere is no evidence of air entrapment or emphysema.\\nThe pleura appears normal.\\nIMPRESSION:\\nCT coronary angio findings reveal no significant stenosis in epicardial coronary arteries.\"}"
