    "description": "Standard clinical NM report template for # HIDA bile leak no collection.",
    "category": "NM",
    "modality": "NM",
    "lines": [
      "HEPATOBILIARY (HIDA) SCINTIGRAPHY",
      "CLINICAL INDICATION: RTA , liver injury ,? Post traumatic bile leak; for evaluation",
      "Technique",
      "Dynamic images of abdomen were acquired after IV injection of Tc99m Mebrofenin for 30mins under gamma camera. Delayed static images acquired upto 24 hours and SPECT CT done at 24 hours .",
      "FINDINGS:-",
      "Liver demonstrates prompt tracer uptake with photopenic (lacerated liver areas) area noted in the superior part of right lobe of liver.",
      "CBD, gallbladder and duodenum is visualised within 5 minutes of study , suggesting good bilioenteric drainage.",
      "Mild grade few  focal tracer activity is noted in the previous photopenic injured right lobe of liver which increases mildly in 24 hour image .",
      "SPECT CT at 24 hours showed no tracer activity in perihepatic , subhepatic or pelvic region , suggesting no intraperitoneal bile collection .",
      "IMPRESSION:",
      "MINIMAL ACTIVE BILE LEAK PROBABLY FROM INJURED INTRAHEPATIC BILIARY DUCTS IN RIGHT LOBE OF LIVER.",
      "FEW SMALL BILIOMAS NOTED IN RIGHT LOBE .",
      "NO  INTRAPERITONEAL BILE COLLECTION.",
      "GOOD BILIOENTERIC DRAINAGE NOTED."
    ],
